18 - (3) The role of the community in the implementation of Protection of Women and Child Victims of Violence as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by:
a. providing communication and information through socialization and education regarding the rights of Women and Children;
b. providing suggestions and input in the formulation of policies related to the Protection of Women and Children;
c. reporting to the competent authorities if there is a violation of the rights of Women and Children;
d. playing an active role in the rehabilitation and social reintegration process for Women and Children;
e. forming family partners at the neighborhood association/community association or village level by the community;
f. forming Women and Child Protection units within community organizations and educational institutions;
g. establishment and management of orphanages;
h. establishment of Child rehabilitation centers;

provision of shelters and/or social houses;

1. job skills training; and

J.
k. providing first aid when violations of the rights of Women and Children occur.
(4) Further provisions regarding community participation shall be regulated by Mayor Regulation.

Article 7

1. Forms of services for Protection of Women as referred to in Article 6 letter a include:  a. legal aid;
b. health services;
c. social rehabilitation services;

d. complaint, consultation and counseling services;
e. social reintegration services; and
f. pre-marital guidance services.

I 11 - 7 - (2) Pre-marital guidance services as referred to in paragraph (1) letter f, shall be implemented by every woman who will enter into marriage.

3. Guidance as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be conducted to provide understanding and knowledge regarding family resilience, health, psychology, religion, social and culture.
4. Guidance as referred to in paragraph (3) shall be implemented by the Regional Apparatus that administers affairs in the field of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection.
5. In implementing guidance as referred to in paragraph (4), the Regional Apparatus may involve:  a. relevant agencies;
b. religious leaders; and c. customary leaders.
6. Further provisions regarding minimum service standards for the protection of Women shall be regulated by Mayor Regulation.

CHAPTER IV

COORDINATION AND COOPERATION

Article 16

1. The implementation of coordination and cooperation for the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence aims to: a. improve efforts to fulfill the rights of Women and Children;
b. improve synergistic and harmonious working relationships; and c. obtain data and information in the implementation of Protection of Women and Children.
2. In order to achieve the objectives as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government cooperates with:
a. other Regional Governments;
b. related agencies;
c. non-governmental institutions;

d. universities; and
e. non-governmental organizations.
3. Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (2) includes: a. exchange of data and information;
b. socialization or legal counseling lectures;
c. rehabilitation of victims of violence; and d. repatriation and social reintegration.

Article 6

Protection of Women includes:
a. services;
b. empowerment;
c. prevention; and d. monitoring.

