(3) In the case of implementation of technical services as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government may establish a task force.

III - 15 - (4) The task force as referred to in paragraph (3) may also carry out institutional strengthening through cooperation and coordination with:
a. KLA task force;

b. KRA task force;
c. schools and/or educational institutions;

d. Children's forum;
e. children's studio;
f. community organizations;
g. Women's organizations; and h. other institutions concerned with the fulfillment of rights and Protection of Children.
5. The task force as referred to in paragraph (4) is a coordinative institution at the city, sub-district and village levels that coordinates policies, programs and activities to realize sub-districts and Child-Friendly villages.
6. Further provisions regarding technical services as referred to in paragraph (3) are regulated by Mayor Regulation.

CHAPTER IV

COORDINATION AND COOPERATION

Article 16

1. The implementation of coordination and cooperation for the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence aims to: a. improve efforts to fulfill the rights of Women and Children;
b. improve synergistic and harmonious working relationships; and c. obtain data and information in the implementation of Protection of Women and Children.
2. In order to achieve the objectives as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government cooperates with:
a. other Regional Governments;
b. related agencies;
c. non-governmental institutions;

d. universities; and
e. non-governmental organizations.
3. Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (2) includes: a. exchange of data and information;
b. socialization or legal counseling lectures;
c. rehabilitation of victims of violence; and d. repatriation and social reintegration.

Article 7

1. Forms of services for Protection of Women as referred to in Article 6 letter a include:  a. legal aid;
b. health services;
c. social rehabilitation services;

d. complaint, consultation and counseling services;
e. social reintegration services; and
f. pre-marital guidance services.

I 11 - 7 - (2) Pre-marital guidance services as referred to in paragraph (1) letter f, shall be implemented by every woman who will enter into marriage.

3. Guidance as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be conducted to provide understanding and knowledge regarding family resilience, health, psychology, religion, social and culture.
4. Guidance as referred to in paragraph (3) shall be implemented by the Regional Apparatus that administers affairs in the field of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection.
5. In implementing guidance as referred to in paragraph (4), the Regional Apparatus may involve:  a. relevant agencies;
b. religious leaders; and c. customary leaders.
6. Further provisions regarding minimum service standards for the protection of Women shall be regulated by Mayor Regulation.

Article 14

(1) Prevention of violations of Children's rights shall be implemented by the Regional Government and the community.  (2) Prevention of violations of Children's rights implemented by the Regional Government as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by:  a. establishing a network;
b. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of prevention based on partnership patterns with the community, private sector, non-governmental organizations; and c. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to Protection of Children.
3. Prevention of violations of Children's rights implemented by the community as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by: a. increasing Children's productivity;

b. developing Children's self-potential;
c. preventing child marriage;
d. reducing maternal and infant mortality rates; and  e. preventing the occurrence of domestic violence.
4. Establishment of a network as referred to in paragraph (2) letter a, includes work partners of the Regional Government in the implementation of prevention of rights violations in the form of family partners.

(5) Further provisions regarding prevention of violations of Children's rights as referred to in paragraph (3), shall be regulated in Mayor Regulation.

